# tools/f/font5x7_choir.rish -- the 5x7 font's witnesses, sung as one roster row.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/f/font5x7_choir.rish
#
# WHY A CHOIR RATHER THAN 45 ROSTER ROWS. Forty-five witnesses cover this font's glyph tables and
# NOT ONE was reached by any pass -- `witness_reach_scan.sh` counted every one `unheard`, the shape
# the row at `20260908.183635` books one room over: a guard's reach is the roster rather than its
# own quality. Forty-five rows would be one rule written forty-five times.
#
# THE FAMILY IS DISCOVERED, NEVER LISTED, and the discovery lives in
# `tools/fixtures/f/font5x7_choir_scan.sh` so the loop is written in the language that has loops.
# Two faults were met writing this and both are recorded there and here, because each reads exactly
# like a pass: a glob assuming a middle segment ran 44 of the 45, and an untrimmed `wc` newline
# reached `sh` as two lines so a family of 45 refused against a bound of 128.

say "font5x7-choir: Style Gauge, Meter -- the family is counted, bounded, and sung."
say "font5x7-choir: Lens TAME -- a corpus of zero is a red rather than a reading."

say "font5x7-choir: the control -- eight behaviors, every refusal planted and then lifted..."
let ctl = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/f/font5x7_choir_control.sh"]
assert ctl.ok else "font5x7-choir: the control refused -- read its own pass/fail lines"
assert ctl.out contains "fail=0" else "font5x7-choir: a planted refusal behaved differently than stated"

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/f/font5x7_choir_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "font5x7-choir: the family refused -- read its own verdict line above"

# invariant: the scan found members at all; an empty corpus reporting success is the one failure
# this choir exists to prevent, and the scan exits non-zero on it rather than printing ok.
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "font5x7-choir: the family did not answer ok"
assert (scan.out contains "members=0") == false else "font5x7-choir: a corpus of zero is a red, never a reading"

# invariant: every discovered member passed; one red fails the choir and names its path.
assert scan.out contains "reds=0" else "font5x7-choir: a 5x7 glyph witness answered RED -- its path is printed above"

say "GREEN: font5x7-choir -- every 5x7 glyph witness discovered, bounded, and sung under one row."
